<!--
---
description: "Research-study version of the Homelessness SBA course (GSU interdisciplinary studies): the course, preceded by the University of Memphis informed-consent form. Students may take part in the study or not; the course is identical either way, and the answer can be changed at any time from Study Consent Form at the bottom of the navigation. For the course without the study, launch hs_course."
category: homelessness
index: 1
lang: en-Latn-US
---
-->

<!--
  RESEARCH CONSENT GATE

  The research deployment's route "/" lands here, not on the course. Three
  states:
  * unanswered -> the IRB form
  * answered but not acknowledged -> a short, neutral acknowledgment
  * acknowledged -> the course itself

  The gates test ANSWERED, never the value: declining changes nothing about
  what the student does, and the activity carries the same credit. The
  acknowledgment reads differently for the two answers only in its heading.

  The same form block is also the last child of the Course (one block, one
  state), so a student can revisit it and change their answer. The course
  itself stays launchable, so the same content serves outside a study with
  no wrapper at all.
-->

<Vertical id="hs_study" title="Homelessness SBA (Research Study)" launchable="true">

<Use ref="hs_irb_consent_form" when="!@hs_irb_consent.value" />

<Vertical id="hs_irb_ack" when="@hs_irb_consent.value && !@hs_irb_ack_done.value">
<Markdown when="@hs_irb_consent.value === 'consented'">
## Thank you

Your course work may be included in the research, always de-identified. You
can change your answer at any time under **Study Consent Form** at the bottom
of the navigation.
</Markdown>
<Markdown when="@hs_irb_consent.value === 'declined'">
## No problem

Your course work stays out of the research. Nothing about the course changes:
same activities, same credit. You can change your answer at any time under
**Study Consent Form** at the bottom of the navigation.
</Markdown>
<Markdown>
This activity is a requirement for your course, and you receive credit for
completing it whether or not you consent to having your work included in
the research.

A few practical notes: we recommend Firefox, Edge, or Google Chrome (Safari
is unsupported); work on one device at a time; and if you run into any
issue, even a minor one, please tell your instructor.
</Markdown>
<ActionButton id="hs_irb_ack_btn" label="Continue to the course">
<SetFieldAction id="hs_irb_ack_set" target="hs_irb_ack_done" field="value" value="acknowledged" />
</ActionButton>
</Vertical>

<Use ref="hs_course" when="@hs_irb_consent.value && @hs_irb_ack_done.value" />

<!-- Flag holder for the acknowledgment, parked unrendered. A LineInput, not
     a Done: SetFieldAction validates against the target field's schema, and
     a plain string can say what happened. -->
<Hidden id="hs_consent_defs">
<LineInput id="hs_irb_ack_done" />
</Hidden>

</Vertical> <!-- hs_study -->
